{
  "name": "Recorder view-model",
  "notes": [
    "Shared contract for the TUI (nexus-tui/src/recorder_view.rs) and NSH (nexus-nsh/src/recorder-view.ts); plan 54 D0.",
    "input.owner is this client's local controller snapshot, or null when this client does not capture. phase is idle|starting|recording|stopping|stopped|interrupted|failed; captured_samples and pending_samples are integer 16 kHz samples; spool is persistent|best-effort|memory|none; recoverable means the local spool can seal an interrupted recording.",
    "input.core is the authoritative Core public state (GET /api/recordings/{id}), or null when no recording exists. Fields are a subset of docs/api.md: id, generation, revision, capture_state, active, durable_offset, final_sample_count, complete, holes, missing_samples, owner.client_id, transcription_state, transcription_progress, reason. reason is display text (clients map Core codes to words).",
    "input.transcript is the durable transcript page plus at most one provisional tail; it never affects the status rows in this fixture.",
    "input.view is modal_open, page (recorder|recent), transcript_follow and seen_interrupted. input.width is wide or compact (narrow header). input.recent is the GET /api/recordings list for the Recent page.",
    "expect.buttons and expect.focus use command ids for actions; jump_live is the one view-only chip id. expect.disabled maps a button id to its reason. null means no value or no row. expect.hint is the last-row key hint.",
    "The audio warning (expect.audio_warning) is a second persistence line; it never replaces the saved-through text.",
    "expect.recent.rows is the expected visible prefix (the list is virtualised); expect.recent.notice is the 50-recording limit row. A recent row uses the Final/Recording/Interrupted/Transcript incomplete status keys plus the gaps suffix.",
    "Recordings stay in Core's state home (recordings/): there is no Save As and no browser download action. Copy transcript is the only export in V1."
  ],
